{"id":"im/vmx4fu1k","kind":"image","position":{"left":48,"top":158,"width":510,"height":475},"fit":"contain","alt":"Current Perigee app: Barnard’s Star A+C comparison, Play comparison button, dates, wavelengths, quality labels and predicted positions"},
{"id":"sh/zq1czy58","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":155,"width":629,"height":37},"text":"1  Choose and play","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/ypsv6t4n","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":200,"width":629,"height":92},"text":"Open a guided case and press Play comparison. The two images alternate in the same position, making small changes easier to spot against nearby stars.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/dojuxoni","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":306,"width":629,"height":37},"text":"2  Check the comparison","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/cnad4jmx","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":351,"width":629,"height":115},"text":"Barnard’s Star is shown on 25 Aug 2025 and 19 Aug 2026 at nearly the same infrared wavelength. Its glow shifts north against the field stars, consistent with the catalog prediction of about seven display pixels (10 arcseconds).","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/bm1cvy5c","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":479,"width":629,"height":37},"text":"3  Explain and keep the evidence","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/ql8b2t4r","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":603,"top":524,"width":629,"height":129},"text":"The learner records what they noticed, what it supports and what is uncertain. After the checks and notes are complete, a reference answer helps them reflect. Their own words remain saved and can be reopened, printed or exported.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/pkzuton6","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":649,"width":1184,"height":24},"text":"Perigee screenshot using NASA/IPAC SPHEREx images. The ring is a catalog prediction; saturation limits precise position measurements.","style":{"fontSize":14,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0}
